# Upstream #326 gap, mirrored deliberately (v0.23.0 pin): the C parser's
# dot-/index-assign paths return WITHOUT the statement-terminator check, so
# trailing tokens after them are silently DISCARDED (not a parse error) —
# unlike every other simple statement. Both sides must agree byte-for-byte;
# if this program starts parse-erroring at a future pin, upstream closed the
# gap and the frontend's exemption (src/frontend.eigs _p_end_statement note)
# should be removed with that bump.
d is {"k": 1}
d.k is 2 3
print of d.k
d.k += 5 6
print of d.k
l is [1]
l[0] is 8 9
print of l[0]
l[0] += 1 4
print of l[0]
